      "starts_from": "Entry of the order or judgment appealed from",
      "source": "court_rule",
      "source_url": "https://www.courts.michigan.gov/siteassets/rules-instructions-administrative-orders/michigan-court-rules/michigan-court-rules.pdf",
      "consequence_of_miss": "The time limit for an appeal of right is jurisdictional; the appeal of right is lost and review is only by application for leave to appeal (MCR 7.204(A)(1), MCR 3.993(B))."
    },
    {
      "requirement_name": "1983 statute of limitations",
      "deadline": "3 years",
      "starts_from": "The time of the injury (Mich. Comp. Laws § 600.5805(2)); federal law fixes when a § 1983 claim accrues",
      "source": "state_statute",
      "source_url": "https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-600-5805",
      "consequence_of_miss": "Not specified as a penalty; Mich. Comp. Laws § 600.5805(1) provides that a person shall not bring or maintain an action to recover damages for injuries to persons or property unless the action is commenced within the period prescribed by that section, which is 3 years for injury to a person (§ 600.5805(2)). 42 U.S.C. § 1983 fixes no limitation period of its own; 42 U.S.C. § 1988(a) supplies state law where federal law is deficient."
    }
  ],
